# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
*.egg-info/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# Environment
.env

# Claude
.claude/settings.local.json
# Native parallel-session worktrees live in-repo here (ADR-61/#107); ignore so they don't
# show as untracked AND so gitignore-respecting walkers (ruff) don't descend into the full
# checkout. pytest is already safe via its default `.*` norecursedirs (dot-dir skip).
.claude/worktrees/

# Session-end closure proposals (ADR-70 Tier-1; ephemeral, reviewed at next /boot —
# the durable record is the eventual `closes [#N]` commit + JOURNAL, ADR-65)
logs/PROPOSALS-*.md
# RETENTION MOVES THEM OUT FROM UNDER THE PATTERN ABOVE ([#626] step A, 2026-09-02).
# `scripts/logs_retention.py` relocates a dated `logs/<STEM>-YYYY-MM-DD.md` into a
# `logs/YYYY-MM/` month bucket. The flat pattern is anchored one level deep, so the moved
# file stops being ignored the instant it is moved: measured after the first live run, 89
# previously-ignored run artifacts appeared as untracked-and-not-ignored. They are the same
# disposable per-run artifacts they were before the move -- the retention rule changes where
# they sit, never what they are -- so the ignore follows them.
logs/*/PROPOSALS-*.md
logs/*/DETECTOR-ERROR-*.md

# Fleet-health digest (ADR-80 mutable — auto-refreshed by fleet_health.py, never committed;
# durable Tier-2 audit record is docs/audits/*.md, committed by audit.py per ADR-80 §3)
logs/FLEET-HEALTH.md

# Enforcement-coverage digest (Informant Organ, Stage-2 enforcement-transfer — read-only
# reporter, auto-refreshed by scripts/enforcement_coverage.py; never committed, same ephemeral
# pattern as FLEET-HEALTH.md. Writing it must never dirty the tree / trip session-end backpressure.)
logs/ENFORCEMENT-COVERAGE.md

# Lived-workflow sandbox operator funnel (Slice A: isolation-proof outcomes; read-only reporter,
# same ephemeral pattern as ENFORCEMENT-COVERAGE — the sandbox writes it, it is never committed).
logs/LIVED-WORKFLOW.md

# Fleet CLAUDE.md boundary-marker drift digest (#312 read-only reporter; auto-refreshed by
# scripts/boundary_report.py, never committed — same ephemeral pattern as FLEET-HEALTH.md.)
logs/BOUNDARY-DRIFT.md

# L5a descriptive analytics digest — hotspot / change-coupling / rot frames ([#384] read-only
# reporter; auto-refreshed by scripts/fleet_analytics.py, never committed — same ephemeral
# pattern as FLEET-HEALTH.md. Frames change on every commit by construction, so committing
# this would churn the tree constantly and trip session-end backpressure.)
logs/FLEET-ANALYTICS.md

# Fleet-parity digest + checker-run JSONL events (#328 read-only checker, WARN-only v1 —
# scripts/fleet_parity.py; same ephemeral pattern as ENFORCEMENT-COVERAGE. The events file
# is append-only, rotation-capped (single .1 backup), gitignored runtime per FR-8/FR-13;
# the durable record is the JOURNAL-pasted verdict table + eventual committed digests.)
logs/FLEET-PARITY.md
logs/PARITY-EVENTS.jsonl
logs/PARITY-EVENTS.jsonl.1

# Hook bypass record ([#808] — scripts/hooks/bounded_hook.py): the run record, the transcript-scan
# cache and the DECLARED-BROKEN declarations, all printed at SessionStart by fleet_health.py. Local
# runtime state, not committed artifacts: the durable finding is the lane audit.
logs/HOOK-BYPASSES*

# Operator-load gauge trend rows ([#270] — one row per fleet_health.py digest run; the
# gauge writes it at SessionStart, so committing it would dirty the tree on every boot,
# exactly as FLEET-HEALTH.md would. Gitignored is the ROW's own wording, not a default:
# "a gitignored logs/OPERATOR-LOAD.csv row per run". The design (2026-07-05 draft) names
# committed promotion a later, separate decision. UPPERCASE-KEBAB stem + honest extension
# per the 2026-07-22 logs/ naming ruling — .csv is a format claim, so it is not restyled.)
logs/OPERATOR-LOAD.csv

# Ecosystem mutable pointers (ADR-80 mutable/durable split — high-churn pointer, not committed;
# durable records are ecosystem/*/history/*.md + docs/audits/*.md, committed by audit.py)
ecosystem/*/state.yaml

# DB-1 — the trend surface (scripts/gen_trend_dashboard.py --write). Regenerate-on-demand,
# never committed, and that is the successor's central design choice rather than a default.
#
# The predecessor it replaces (ecosystem/conformance.html) is a COMMITTED generated artifact,
# so it can be — and measurably is — stale: the live audit store carried
# "conformance-dashboard: 5d stale" while this generator was being written. Committing this
# page would inherit exactly that disease, and would additionally need a freshness gate to
# police a staleness that only exists because the file is committed. A page regenerated from
# the store on demand cannot be stale, so no gate is owed and none was added.
#
# It also holds no durable signal of its own (ADR-80 mutable/durable split): every point is a
# derived view over git and logs/TELEMETRY.db, so the durable record is the store, exactly as
# the state.yaml entry above reasons.
ecosystem/trends.html

# Session-end gate override (ADR-85) — ephemeral local signal + audit log, never committed.
# The token is a HEAD-bound one-shot the Stop-hook pure-reads; OVERRIDES.md is the local
# override-rate audit trail (matches the logs/PROPOSALS-* / FLEET-HEALTH ephemeral pattern).
logs/.session-override-token
logs/OVERRIDES.md

# Coherence forgotten-version-bump nudge log (CLAUDE.md §9 — non-blocking hook that always
# exits 0; this is its ephemeral append-only record, never committed; same ephemeral pattern
# as logs/PROPOSALS-* / FLEET-HEALTH / OVERRIDES). The durable signal is the reconciled_versions
# audit check + the eventual version bump in git history.
logs/COHERENCE-NUDGE.log

# [#529] leg 2 — the Stage-1 telemetry store. Machine-local measurement of the gate mesh; the
# durable signal is what a reader derives from it, not the file.
#
# THE GLOB, NOT THE BARE NAME, and this is measured rather than defensive. The store is opened
# in WAL mode (memo line 52, telemetry_emit.WAL_PRAGMAS), and WAL keeps two sidecars alive for
# as long as a connection is open:
#     files while a connection is OPEN: TELEMETRY.db  TELEMETRY.db-shm  TELEMETRY.db-wal
#     files after a clean close:        TELEMETRY.db
# They vanish on a clean close and SURVIVE a crashed writer or a concurrent reader — which is
# precisely the state WAL exists to support here, since the point is concurrent hook and lane
# writers. A bare `logs/TELEMETRY.db` would leave a stray `-wal` dirtying `git status` and
# tripping session-end backpressure: the exact failure this leg was filed to prevent.
logs/TELEMETRY.db*

# Vendored Pyright langserver for the reverse-dep oracle (#193, ADR-89). The version is
# pinned in package.json + package-lock.json (committed); the heavy node_modules tree is
# rebuilt per-checkout via `npm install` (bootstrap documented in scripts/reverse_dep_oracle.py).
node_modules/

# OS
*.tmp
*.bak

# Personal scratch / temp work (unrelated to repo content)
temp/

# [#563] one-way Backlog.md view layer -- disposable, regenerated per read, never
# committed. BELT-AND-BRACES ONLY: scripts/export_backlog_view.py writes a .gitignore
# containing * at the export root as the FIRST file of every export, so the tree is
# already self-ignoring with or without this entry (and so is a sibling export dir
# outside the repo). Landed because the row's literal wording names it.
.backlog-view/

# DISPATCH ARTIFACTS -- what `Dispatch-Codespace` leaves in the container's clone (G0, [#632]).
#
# The container's workdir IS this repo, so every file the transport ships in or the runner
# writes lands at THIS repo's root: the runner and the contract are cp'd in, the log and the
# diag dir are created at start, and `receipt.json` is written at the end. A lane commits and
# pushes FROM inside that container, so without these lines a `git add -A` sweeps the dispatch
# transport's own scaffolding into the lane's commit -- and a dirty tree is also how a finished
# lane is told apart from a wedged one.
#
# LOCAL RUNS ARE UNAFFECTED and that was checked rather than assumed: the receipt is cp'd BACK
# to the system temp dir (`GetTempPath()/receipt-<slug>.json`), never into the operator's
# checkout. These entries exist for the container side alone.
#
# `receipt.json` is anchored to the ROOT (leading slash) deliberately -- it is a generic name,
# and an unanchored rule would silently swallow a real `receipt.json` a child repo or a fixture
# tree might legitimately carry.
/receipt.json
/dispatch-run.sh
/dispatch-run.log
/dispatch-detach.log
/dispatch-diag/
# The contract itself is cp'd in under its own filename. A lane contract at the repo ROOT is
# never legitimate -- ADR-101 hermetization refuses one there -- so anchoring the pattern to
# the root cannot hide a real artifact.
#
# WHY GITIGNORED RATHER THAN DELETED (measured 2026-09-01, lane-632 second run; merged from
# worktree-lane-632-codespace-proof): `dispatch-run.log` is actively written by the in-flight
# session's stdout redirect and `dispatch-run.sh` is the running parent script. Deleting either
# mid-run risks the harness's own idle-based fuse misreading file-growth and killing a live
# session. Ignoring them is therefore the safe disposition, not merely the tidy one.
/LANE-*.md

# DISPATCH TRACE STREAM (Lane h0, `LANE-h0-trace.md`; `scripts/trace_writer.py`) -- one
# readable file per dispatch under logs/prompts/, reusing receipt.json's own fields rather
# than inventing a new format. Never committed: same ephemeral-organ-output pattern as
# logs/FLEET-HEALTH.md above -- a local artifact `fleet_health.py` counts, not a durable
# record. Not anchored to root: the home is `logs/prompts/` by convention, not a bare
# top-level name a hermetization rule needs to disambiguate.
logs/prompts/
# SPINE / MOMENT RECEIPTS (lane-l1-spine-moments; scripts/dodo.py, `telemetry_emit.py wrap --receipt`) -- one
# machine-written file per stage or organ run: the doit TARGET, "receipt present = step done" (DECLARE-NIGHT N2).
# Follows the `logs/prompts/` precedent above (RECON-NIGHT 2026-09-20 s2 shape (a)): under `logs/`, in a
# sub-directory, gitignored, so it never meets the hermetization gate. Undated names: logs_retention would
# move a dated one out from under its own doit target.
logs/receipts/
